9. SEALED-PAGE DESIGN PRINCIPLE
======================================================================

For project identification purposes, the RIAPS architecture documented in
this repository is centered on the following principle:

    Historical pagination should behave as an append-only archive rather
    than a continuously rebalanced window over newly published content.

A RIAPS implementation may use immutable, monotonically increasing post
identifiers and persistent page boundaries represented conceptually by:

    archive identity
    page number
    start post ID
    end post ID

A completed archive page can then be reconstructed from its stable ID
range together with the applicable archive predicate.

The detailed technical specification is provided in the project's
technical documentation.


